{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Canonical.ModularHamiltonianDoubledBridge\nimport InfoGeometry.Canonical.ModularSuperchargeClosure\nimport InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelativeModularPotential\nimport InfoGeometry.Canonical.OperatorDictionary\nimport InfoGeometry.Meta.Architecture\nimport Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Algebra.Exponential\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Canonical.HestenesModularBregman\n\nReal doubled Hestenes modular beta flows and operatorial Bregman readouts.\n\nThis file implements the trace-free root layer behind:\n\n* `Delta - I` as deviation from the modular identity sector;\n* `Kmod = -log Delta` as modular Hamiltonian / surprisal generator;\n* `beta ↦ exp(-beta • Kmod)` as the untraced modular exponential family;\n* operatorial Bregman divergence as convex-potential readout from a differential.\n\nNo density matrices, no trace partition function, and no type-I normalization are\nintroduced here.\n\nThe existing phase axis\n\n  phaseAxisK = J ∘ epsilon = complex_i = clockAxis\n\nis not the modular Hamiltonian. We keep the names separate:\n\n* `phaseAxisK` / `clockAxis` : real doubled Hestenes internal complex axis;\n* `Kmod`                    : modular Hamiltonian / surprisal generator;\n* `Delta`                   : modular operator / beta-flow endpoint.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.HestenesModularBregman\n\nopen InfoGeometry.Krein\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.OperatorDictionary\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.ModularHamiltonianDoubledBridge\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelativeModularPotential\n\nsection Core\n\nvariable {E : Type 0}\nvariable [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E]\n\nlocal notation \"H₂\" => DoubledSpace E\nlocal notation \"EndH\" => H₂ →L[ℝ] H₂\n\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedRing EndH := inferInstance\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedAlgebra ℝ EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : IsTopologicalRing EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : CompleteSpace EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : SMulCommClass ℝ EndH EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : IsScalarTower ℝ EndH EndH := inferInstance\n\n/--\nThe modular identity operator.\n\nIn type-III language, the identity is not removed. What fails is a faithful\nnormal trace/finite partition function by default, not the unital identity.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def modularIdentity : EndH :=\n  1\n\n/-- The modular identity is the continuous-linear identity map. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularIdentity_eq_id :\n    modularIdentity (E := E) = ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ H₂ := by\n  rfl\n\n/--\n`Delta - I`: deviation of a modular operator from the identity/reference sector.\n\nThis is not a trace regularization and not a density-matrix normalization.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def modularDeviation (Delta : EndH) : EndH :=\n  Delta - modularIdentity (E := E)\n\n/-- The identity sector has zero modular deviation. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularDeviation_identity :\n    modularDeviation (E := E) (modularIdentity (E := E)) = 0 := by\n  simp [modularDeviation, modularIdentity]\n\n/--\nUntraced modular beta flow generated by a bounded modular Hamiltonian `Kmod`.\n\nThis is the safe bounded-operator root:\n\n  beta ↦ exp(-beta • Kmod)\n\nNo logarithm, trace, or partition function is assumed here.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def modularBetaFlow (Kmod : EndH) (beta : ℝ) : EndH :=\n  NormedSpace.exp ((-beta) • Kmod)\n\n/-- At `beta = 0`, the modular beta flow is the identity. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularBetaFlow_zero (Kmod : EndH) :\n    modularBetaFlow (E := E) Kmod 0 = modularIdentity (E := E) := by\n  simp [modularBetaFlow, modularIdentity]\n\n/-- At `beta = 1`, the modular beta flow is `exp(-Kmod)`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularBetaFlow_one (Kmod : EndH) :\n    modularBetaFlow (E := E) Kmod 1 = NormedSpace.exp (-Kmod) := by\n  simp [modularBetaFlow]\n\n/-- Endpoint modular operator associated to a bounded modular Hamiltonian. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def modularDeltaFromHamiltonian (Kmod : EndH) : EndH :=\n  modularBetaFlow (E := E) Kmod 1\n\n/-- Readback for `modularDeltaFromHamiltonian`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularDeltaFromHamiltonian_eq_exp_neg (Kmod : EndH) :\n    modularDeltaFromHamiltonian (E := E) Kmod = NormedSpace.exp (-Kmod) := by\n  simp [modularDeltaFromHamiltonian, modularBetaFlow]\n\n/-- Beta-flow deviation from the identity sector. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def modularBetaDeviation (Kmod : EndH) (beta : ℝ) : EndH :=\n  modularDeviation (E := E) (modularBetaFlow (E := E) Kmod beta)\n\n/-- The beta-flow deviation vanishes at `beta = 0`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularBetaDeviation_zero (Kmod : EndH) :\n    modularBetaDeviation (E := E) Kmod 0 = 0 := by\n  simp [modularBetaDeviation, modularDeviation, modularBetaFlow, modularIdentity]\n\n/-- The beta-one deviation is exactly `exp(-Kmod) - I`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularBetaDeviation_one (Kmod : EndH) :\n    modularBetaDeviation (E := E) Kmod 1\n      = NormedSpace.exp (-Kmod) - modularIdentity (E := E) := by\n  simp [modularBetaDeviation, modularDeviation, modularBetaFlow]\n\n/--\nCanonical Tomita modular Hamiltonian readback.\n\nThis is only a name for the bounded owner expression already carried by\n`ModularSuperchargeClosure.canonicalTomitaLogData`: `Kmod = -deltaLog`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def canonicalTomitaKmod\n    (CIK : CertifiedInverseKernel H₂) : EndH :=\n  -((ModularSuperchargeClosure.canonicalTomitaLogData (E := E) CIK).deltaLog)\n\n/--\nFor the canonical Tomita package, the beta-one flow of `Kmod = -deltaLog`\nrecovers the owned modular operator `Delta`.\n\nThis is the rooted `K = -log Delta` readback already proved in the doubled lane.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem canonicalTomita_betaFlow_one_eq_Delta\n    (CIK : CertifiedInverseKernel H₂) :\n    modularBetaFlow (E := E) (canonicalTomitaKmod (E := E) CIK) 1\n      = (ModularSuperchargeClosure.canonicalTomitaLogData (E := E) CIK).Delta := by\n  unfold modularBetaFlow canonicalTomitaKmod\n  simpa using canonicalTomita_modularHamiltonian_exp_neg_eq_Delta (E := E) CIK\n\n/--\nThe canonical modular deviation is the beta-one deviation of the canonical\nTomita modular Hamiltonian.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem canonicalTomita_deviation_eq_beta_one_deviation\n    (CIK : CertifiedInverseKernel H₂) :\n    modularDeviation (E := E) ((ModularSuperchargeClosure.canonicalTomitaLogData (E := E) CIK).Delta)\n      = modularBetaDeviation (E := E) (canonicalTomitaKmod (E := E) CIK) 1 := by\n  unfold modularBetaDeviation\n  rw [canonicalTomita_betaFlow_one_eq_Delta]\n\n/--\nPositive Hilbert expectation readout of an operator at a doubled state.\n\nThis is a scalar state-operator pairing, not an operator product.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def hilbertExpectationAt\n    (psi : H₂) (A : EndH) : ℝ :=\n  ⟪psi, A psi⟫_ℝ\n\n/--\nKrein expectation readout of an operator at a doubled state.\n\nThis is the indefinite-pairing analogue of state-operator evaluation.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def kreinExpectationAt\n    (psi : H₂) (A : EndH) : ℝ :=\n  KreinSpace.kreinInner (H := H₂) psi (A psi)\n\n/-- Zero Hilbert expectation readout. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem hilbertExpectationAt_zero (psi : H₂) :\n    hilbertExpectationAt (E := E) psi 0 = 0 := by\n  simp [hilbertExpectationAt]\n\n/-- Zero Krein expectation readout. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem kreinExpectationAt_zero (psi : H₂) :\n    kreinExpectationAt (E := E) psi 0 = 0 := by\n  simp [kreinExpectationAt]\n\n/--\nOperatorial Bregman divergence from a potential and a differential.\n\n`dPhi Y` is the cotangent/readout at the base point `Y`.\n\nThis is the trace-free convex-duality root shape:\n\n  DΦ(X,Y) = Φ(X) - Φ(Y) - dΦ(Y)(X - Y)\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def operatorBregman\n    (Phi : EndH → ℝ)\n    (dPhi : EndH → EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (X Y : EndH) : ℝ :=\n  Phi X - Phi Y - dPhi Y (X - Y)\n\n/-- Bregman divergence vanishes on the diagonal. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem operatorBregman_self\n    (Phi : EndH → ℝ)\n    (dPhi : EndH → EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (X : EndH) :\n    operatorBregman (E := E) Phi dPhi X X = 0 := by\n  simp [operatorBregman]\n\n/--\nSouriau untraced operatorial exponential family.\n\nGiven a Lie-generator readout `Jhat : g → EndH`, the untraced beta family is\n\n  exp(-beta • Jhat xi)\n\nNo trace, no partition function, and no normalization is assumed.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def souriauUntracedExponential\n    {g : Type*}\n    (Jhat : g → EndH)\n    (beta : ℝ)\n    (xi : g) : EndH :=\n  modularBetaFlow (E := E) (Jhat xi) beta\n\n/-- At beta zero, the Souriau untraced exponential is the identity. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem souriauUntracedExponential_zero\n    {g : Type*}\n    (Jhat : g → EndH)\n    (xi : g) :\n    souriauUntracedExponential (E := E) Jhat 0 xi = modularIdentity (E := E) := by\n  simp [souriauUntracedExponential, modularBetaFlow_zero]\n\n/-- Souriau untraced beta deviation from identity. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def souriauUntracedDeviation\n    {g : Type*}\n    (Jhat : g → EndH)\n    (beta : ℝ)\n    (xi : g) : EndH :=\n  modularDeviation (E := E) (souriauUntracedExponential (E := E) Jhat beta xi)\n\n/-- Souriau untraced deviation vanishes at beta zero. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem souriauUntracedDeviation_zero\n    {g : Type*}\n    (Jhat : g → EndH)\n    (xi : g) :\n    souriauUntracedDeviation (E := E) Jhat 0 xi = 0 := by\n  simp [souriauUntracedDeviation, souriauUntracedExponential,\n    modularDeviation, modularBetaFlow, modularIdentity]\n\nend Core\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.HestenesModularBregman\n","mtime":1778592758555}